        <item>
            <title>1.1.0</title>
            <pubDate>Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:25:55 -0400</pubDate>
            <link>https://jack.novor.dev</link>
            <sparkle:fullReleaseNotesLink>https://jack.novor.dev/releases/v1.1.0</sparkle:fullReleaseNotesLink>
            <sparkle:version>635</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.1.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<p>Control the volume of each app from your menu bar, with clearer dictation and a movable live caption that stays out of your way.</p>
<h3>Sound Controls</h3>
<ul>
<li>Adjust or mute individual apps, choose their speakers, and watch live audio levels from the menu bar. Per-app controls require macOS 14.2 or later</li>
<li>Use Solo to hear one app, Call Mode to lower other audio during calls, or save a favourite mix as a sound scene</li>
<li>See and control playback in Spotify and Music, and adjust individual browser tabs with the optional Jack Tab Volume extension</li>
<li>Choose how other apps sound while you dictate, including lower volume and four Muffle styles</li>
</ul>
<h3>Clearer, Faster Dictation</h3>
<ul>
<li>The English speech model stays ready between dictations, with a final accuracy pass when you finish speaking</li>
<li>Quiet microphone audio is levelled more carefully, and Jack prefers the Mac's built-in microphone over AirPods unless you choose another input</li>
<li>Text cleanup uses your vocabulary and learned corrections, and can fall back to Apple Intelligence on supported Macs when the local cleanup model is unavailable</li>
<li>Drag the live caption anywhere on screen. Words appear at a steadier pace, and Jack remembers where you leave it</li>
<li>Start another dictation immediately after finishing, with more reliable pasting and spacing between consecutive dictations</li>
</ul>
<h3>Everyday Fixes</h3>
<ul>
<li>Fixed a recurring clipboard pause when working with a large history</li>
<li>Press Space to open or close Quick Look for the selected clip</li>
<li>Improved sound-device handling to prevent repeated audio restarts, crackling, and slowdowns</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
